---
/**
 * Standing notice above the figures on any paper that shows working figures
 * rather than the published versions.
 *
 * The wording is Jackson's, in his own voice. Do not reword it.
 */
---

<aside class="figure-notice" aria-labelledby="figure-notice-heading">
  <h3 id="figure-notice-heading">About these figures</h3>
  <p>
    These are working figures — made quickly, to look at something. They have not been peer
    reviewed and are not the versions that appear in the published papers. I'm putting them up
    because I'd rather people see the work than not.
  </p>
  <p class="rights">
    Please email me if you want the originals of any of these. The journals control the licenses
    for any published figures.
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .figure-notice {
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-2);
    border-left-width: 4px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--accent-2-wash);
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    margin-block: 2rem 1.5rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
  }

  p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .rights {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
  }
</style>
